 This is a math problem, so please don't explain the . actual : penguin : behavior, just the computations. 36 penguins are sunbathing. One-third jump in the ocean, another one-third go to eat. So, the total fraction that left is 1/3 + 1/3 = 2/3. The remaining fraction is 1 - 2/3 = 1/3. Therefore, the number of penguins left is 36 * 1/3 = 12. The answer is 12. \boxed{12}
