 Okay, let me try to figure out this math problem. So Travis starts with 61 apps on his tablet. Then he deletes 9 apps that he doesn't use anymore. After deleting those, he downloads 18 more apps. The question is asking how many apps are on his tablet now.

Alright, let's break it down step by step. First, he had 61 apps. Then he deletes 9. So deleting apps would mean subtracting from the original number. So 61 minus 9. Let me calculate that. 61 minus 9 is... 52? Wait, 61 minus 10 would be 51, so adding 1 back makes it 52. Yeah, that seems right.

Then, after deleting those 9, he downloads 18 more. Downloading apps would mean adding to the current number. So now it's 52 plus 18. Let's do that math. 52 plus 18. Hmm, 50 plus 10 is 60, and 2 plus 8 is 10, so total is 70? Wait, no, that's not right. Wait 52 + 18. Break it down: 52 + 10 is 62, then +8 more is 70. Yes, that's correct. So 52 + 18 equals 70.

So starting with 61, subtract 9 to get 52, then add 18 to get 70. Therefore, Travis now has 70 apps on his tablet. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes. Original number: 61. Delete 9: 61-9=52. Then download 18: 52+18=70. Yep, that all adds up. I think that's the right answer.
